From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:19:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display/msm: dsi-phy-7nm: Add SM6450
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Document the DSI PHY on SM6450. It is the 5nm v4.3 PHY that SM8450
carries, at the same address and with the same supply load, but SM6450
has only the one.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/dsi-phy-7nm.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/dsi-phy-7nm.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/dsi-phy-7nm.yaml
index 1ca820a50..5f043d629 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/dsi-phy-7nm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/dsi-phy-7nm.yaml
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ properties:
       - qcom,sar2130p-dsi-phy-5nm
       - qcom,sc7280-dsi-phy-7nm
       - qcom,sm6375-dsi-phy-7nm
+      - qcom,sm6450-dsi-phy-5nm
       - qcom,sm8350-dsi-phy-5nm
       - qcom,sm8450-dsi-phy-5nm
       - qcom,sm8550-dsi-phy-4nm
